      {
        "id": 133666,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-24T14:33:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Expat's LNR only affect the actual target of the damage, and take effect if the target is dealt damage or not.</p><p>Anytime damage is redirected the final target is treated as the target of that damage.</p><p>Korruption deals each target damage. &nbsp;Then he looks and sees who actually took damage, and each of those targets takes 1 toxic damage, so Immutus takes 1 toxic after eating all the pings.</p><p>Knyfe's is worded to make that decision take place after each damage, so each time you deal 1 that initial damage you decide whether to hit that target again or not.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The key is Korruption has \"then\" making the second part take place after the first resolves.</p><p>Knyfe's is written as a static effect, it takes place as long as the card is in play, and for each target damaged that way.</p><p>So Incidental Contact will jack up Immutus much more than Korruption will.</p>",
