        "raw": "<p>Expat&#39;s LNR only affect the actual target of the damage, and take effect if the target is dealt damage or not.</p><p>Anytime damage is redirected the final target is treated as the target of that damage.</p><p>Korruption deals each target damage. &nbsp;Then he looks and sees who actually took damage, and each of those targets takes 1 toxic damage, so Immutus takes 1 toxic after eating all the pings.</p><p>Knyfe&#39;s is worded to make that decision take place after each damage, so each time you deal 1 that initial damage you decide whether to hit that target again or not.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The key is Korruption has &quot;then&quot; making the second part take place after the first resolves.</p><p>Knyfe&#39;s is written as a static effect, it takes place as long as the card is in play, and for each target damaged that way.</p><p>So Incidental Contact will jack up Immutus much more than Korruption will.</p>",
